-- DEV-ONLY sample data so the frontend has something to render and click through.
-- Loaded only when the "dev" profile adds classpath:db/seed to spring.flyway.locations
-- (see application-dev.yml) — never part of the production migration set.
--
-- Every account below logs in with password: Admin@123 (same hash as V2's admin).
-- Times are relative to the moment this migration runs, so "upcoming" slots really are in the future
-- on a fresh DB. They use LOCALTIMESTAMP because the app itself writes these TIMESTAMP columns as
-- wall-clock time in the JVM's zone (the JDBC session zone Flyway also runs in): slots land at
-- 09:00/14:00 local time whether the backend runs on a Vietnam-time machine or in a UTC container.

